Here's the debounce helper I keep in our utils folder. It preserves `this` and forwards all args, and I use it on a search box with a 250ms wait. Does this look solid to you, or am I missing something obvious?

```js
function debounce(fn, wait) {
  let timer;
  return function (...args) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), wait);
  };
}
```

